      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T17:50:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t understand the existence of this enum, nor all the switching. All of these can be better passed in to the constructor directly down in the DEF_GM. Currently the constructor is taking this enum and then this class is expanding that into some set parameter pack. This is very strange organization, just let the caller set the parameters (and the test name, etc).\n\nThis is in fact why all the `sets` on SkFontArguments return SkFontArguments\u0026, so that a new one can be created and set up and then passed directly, without needing to name the temporary. Likewise PaletteOverride can be compile time brace initialized, especially when `colorOverrides*` aren\u0027t std::vectors but just pointers.\n\nIn other words, just pass the `const char* name` and `const SkFontArguments\u0026 args` directly to the constructor and set them up in the parameter list of the constructor call in DEF_GM below.",
      "revId": "88736c5aa3a705d561b690795ad8cb089f894daa",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
