      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T17:50:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see. So FreeType currently has a way to get the palette data, select a palette index, and set the foreground color. But it doesn\u0027t currently have a way to just set the palette. With the axes we just resolve them, send them off to FreeType and they\u0027re all just set.\n\nSince the web has a thing about setting palette data, perhaps this means we should suggest that FreeType add a means of setting palette entries much like this (and much like setting axes in a variable font).\n\nFor now, though, this is fine. Might want to comment here that as of right now FreeType doesn\u0027t allow setting individual palette entry values, so we need to keep track of the overrides.",
      "revId": "88736c5aa3a705d561b690795ad8cb089f894daa",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
